    {id="auto-theme-it-states-a-lesson-shown-by-the-character-s-actions-08ae58", subject="Reading / ELA", skill="theme", priority=5, prompt="Why is “Keep trying and learn from mistakes” a stronger theme than “Paper airplanes can fly”?", answer="It states a lesson shown by the character’s actions.", hint="Ask which choice could apply beyond this one story.", explanation="A theme is a broader lesson or message, not just a fact or detail from the story.", choices={"It states a lesson shown by the character’s actions.","It repeats one object from the story.","It describes only where the story happens."}},
